  "body": "`late_fee` in `src/berth_fee.py` always returns 0, so a boat that overstays pays nothing. A late fee should apply once a grace period ends. Neither the length of the grace period nor the amount of the fee is stated in the repository or the vault; both are the harbour board's calls.\n\n**Delivers:** `late_fee(days_late)` returns 0 while `days_late` is within the grace period and the board-set fee once it has ended, replacing the constant 0 at `src/berth_fee.py:2`; the signature at `src/berth_fee.py:1` stays. The grace length and fee amount are unresolved (see below).\n\n**Test contract:** Failing tests first, against `late_fee`, with values taken from the board's answer: returns 0 for no lateness; returns 0 on the last day of the grace period; returns the fee on the first day after it; a longer overstay returns what the board's fee shape dictates. The repository has no tests yet, so this task starts that surface.\n\n**Files:** `src/berth_fee.py` (modified); a new test module for `late_fee` (created).\n\n## Flow-out\n\n- [ ] Touched area/subsystem profiles updated with what changed\n- [ ] Prover-validated assumptions captured as session candidates (durable at flush)\n- [ ] New decisions / lessons / follow-ups surfaced during the build recorded\n\n## Refine \u2014 unresolved\n\n**Question:** What has the harbour board set for the late fee: how many days is the grace period, and what is the fee once it ends (the amount, and whether it is flat or charged per day)?\n\n**Evidence gathered:** `src/berth_fee.py:1-2` is a stub with no constants, rates or currency. No other module in `src/` or `README.md` mentions fees, lateness or grace periods, and there are no tests or callers. In the vault, `lore areas` lists no areas and searches for ADRs, decisions and lessons return nothing. Searches on late fee, grace period, overstay, tariff, penalty and harbour board find only this task. [[spec/fixture-berth-fee-spec]] and [[task/fixture-berth-fee-spec-the-slice]] (the related task) are placeholders with no fee content. The captured prose above assigns both values to the board.\n\n**Recommended answer:** No value is recommended: nothing in the code or vault supports a number, and picking one would invent board policy. Get both values from the board, then answer here. Once they are in, the Delivers and Test contract can take them without further design, and the task can be promoted.\n**Answer:** The grace period is 3 days, but the fee amount is up to the harbour board and has not been decided yet.\n",
